* Wed Sep 30 2026 Jeremy Melanson <1080872+zish@users.noreply.github.com> - 1.1.0-1
- API versioning (docs/58). This daemon now speaks a declared range of wire
  formats -- API 1 to 1 today -- and agrees one with the app at auth instead of
  announcing a number nothing read. **No app update is required by this
  release**: an app that sends no range is taken to speak API 1, which is what
  every app built before negotiation existed speaks.
- A refusal is machine-readable: err=api_unsupported plus reason, both ranges,
  and this package's name and version, so the app can tell "update the app" from
  "update the host package" and name what is installed.
- PACKAGE_VERSION is stamped at build time by %install and verified there. A
  repo checkout reports "0-dev", which is honest about being unpackaged.
- The connection profile carries api_min/api_max and host_package_version, so
  the app can read the range before it opens a socket. Note host_package rather
  than package: "package" already means the ANDROID app id in waydroid-pwd's
  profile, and one name for two things would have been a trap.
- The org.bluez.Agent1 path moved to /waydroid/ext/btd/agent in 1.0.1; noted
  here because nothing outside the daemon names it and it is easy to miss.

* Wed Sep 30 2026 Jeremy Melanson <1080872+zish@users.noreply.github.com> - 1.0.1-1
- Follows the app id rename: DEFAULT_PACKAGE is com.systemhalted.bluetooth,
  where it was com.systemhalted.bluetooth. This is load-bearing rather than cosmetic --
  the daemon writes the app's connection profile into <data>/data/<package>/
  files/btd.json, so a wrong constant means the app can never find the daemon.
  1.0.0 on a host with the renamed app logs "com.systemhalted.bluetooth is not
  installed yet; will keep offering the profile", forever.
- Installing this retires the interim /etc/systemd/system/waydroid-btd.service.d/
  package.conf drop-in that passed --package to bridge the gap. Remove the
  drop-in in the same transaction, not before.
- The org.bluez.Agent1 object path is now /waydroid/ext/btd/agent, where it was
  /com/systemhalted/btd/agent. Internal: BlueZ registers whatever path it is given and
  nothing outside this daemon names it. Renamed so no private LAN domain is left
  anywhere in the D-Bus surface.

* Tue Sep 22 2026 Jeremy Melanson <1080872+zish@users.noreply.github.com> - 1.0.0-1
- First package. Host-side BlueZ management for Waydroid's Android, exporting
  an org.bluez.Agent1 so pairing prompts can be answered from inside the
  container (docs/50).
- The Android half is deliberately a separate modification: an APK with its
  own build and release cadence, which should not reissue this daemon.
